%% Calendar module flow, drawn from server/src/calendar (checked 2026-10-16).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Client / Owner
    participant Ctrl as CalendarController
    participant Svc as CalendarService
    participant Tools as CalendarTools (AI tools)
    participant Sync as CalendarSyncService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant GAPI as Google Calendar API v3

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
    note over Client, DB: 1. CRUD on the local calendar
    Client->>Ctrl: POST / GET / PATCH / DELETE /calendar
    Ctrl->>Svc: createEvent / getEvents / updateEvent / deleteEvent
    Svc->>DB: local_calendars, calendar_sync_states = DIRTY on create and update
    alt delete, event already on Google
        Svc->>DB: deleted_at = now, sync state DIRTY
    else delete, never pushed
        Svc->>DB: delete the row
    end
    Ctrl-->>Client: { statusCode, message, data }
    end

    rect rgb(245, 245, 220)
    note over Tools, DB: 2. AI tools
    Tools->>Svc: get_calendar_events, create_calendar_event (run in the chat)
    Tools->>Svc: update_calendar_event, delete_calendar_event (only after POST /ai-agent/actions/:id/confirm)
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
    note over Client, GAPI: 3. One-way push, local to Google
    Sync->>Sync: cron from CALENDAR_SYNC_CRON (default every 5 minutes), or POST /calendar/sync
    Sync->>DB: Google tokens (decrypted), DIRTY sync states with their events
    note over Sync: no tokens, or a run in progress: skip (data null)
    loop each DIRTY event
        alt soft-deleted
            Sync->>GAPI: events.delete (404 / 410 ignored)
            Sync->>DB: delete the local row
        else no google_event_id
            Sync->>GAPI: events.insert (id = local UUID without dashes, 409 means already created)
            Sync->>DB: SYNCED, etag, last_synced_at
        else has google_event_id
            Sync->>GAPI: events.patch (summary, description, location, start, end)
            alt 404 / 410, deleted on Google
                Sync->>DB: clear google_event_id, SYNCED (not pushed again)
            else ok
                Sync->>DB: SYNCED, etag, last_synced_at
            end
        end
    end
    note over Sync, DB: SYNCED only if the sync state was not edited meanwhile, else it stays DIRTY
    Sync-->>Client: POST /calendar/sync returns { pushed, deleted, removedRemotely, failed }
    end
